role: Hydrologist; these school models do not predict real floods.", "observable_behaviours": "Compare the Two Field Reports: align source ID, conditions, observations and missing fields side by side; identify which differences can be compared fairly; Build a Matched Runoff Comparison: compare the trays, keep the input and slope conditions matched, collect runoff separately and log source-specific readings; Calculate Runoff Across Three Trials: calculate means 160 mL and 100 mL; compute 64% and 40% runoff; report the 24-percentage-point gap", "role_work_context": "A watershed or hydrology team needs fair rainfall-runoff comparisons and repeated data before giving advice about river flow, erosion and possible flood impacts.", "typical_work_activities": "Compare two field reports and identify non-matched conditions; Set up a matched bare-soil versus leaf-cover runoff comparison; Average three model runoff trials for each condition; Compute runoff percentages and state the percentage-point difference without overclaiming soil loss", "role_output_evidence": "Field-report comparison; Matched-tray method and reading log; Three-trial average calculation; Runoff percentage and limitation report; Learning modules: RMR-CAP-L03-M01 - Compare the Two Field Reports (Core, step 1), RMR-CAP-L03-M02 - Build a Matched Runoff Comparison (Important, step 2), RMR-CAP-L03-M03 - Calculate Runoff Across Three Trials (Important, step 3)", "primary_riasec": "I", "secondary_riasec": "R", "tertiary_riasec": "C", "riasec_reason": "Investigative work interprets rainfall and runoff; Realistic work involves physical river and land conditions; Conventional methods require consistent trial records and units.", "degree_gate": "Preferred", "direct_degree_mapping": "B.Tech. Civil Engineering; B.Sc. Geography; B.Sc. Geology; M.Sc. Hydrology", "riasec_code_string": "IRC", "aptitude_profile": {"verbal_reasoning": 67, "logical_reasoning": 86, "numerical_reasoning": 87, "data_interpretation": 91, "pattern_recognition": 80, "spatial_reasoning": 78}, "big_five_profile": {"openness": 5, "conscientiousness": 5, "extraversion": 2, "agreeableness": 3, "emotional_stability": 4}, "work_values_profile": {"impact": 5, "status": 3, "autonomy": 4, "security": 4, "financial": 3, "lifestyle": 4, "creativity": 4, "leadership": 2}, "aptitude_assessment": {"areas": ["Data Interpretation", "Numerical Reasoning", "Logical Reasoning"], "rationale": "Rain & Flood Expert uses data interpretation, numerical reasoning, logical reasoning to compare two field reports and identify non-matched conditions, set up a matched bare-soil versus leaf-cover runoff comparison, and interpret source-based records. These priorities are proposed role demands, not measured learner aptitude."}, "big5_assessment": {"traits": ["Openness", "Conscientiousness", "Emotional Stability"], "rationale": "Rain & Flood Expert benefits from openness, conscientiousness, emotional stability when performing set up a matched bare-soil versus leaf-cover runoff comparison and following through on runoff percentage and limitation report. Traits guide supportive coaching, not exclusion."}, "work_values_assessment": {"values": ["Impact", "Autonomy", "Security"], "rationale": "This pathway may reward impact, autonomy, security through the work of compare two field reports and identify non-matched conditions and producing a clear field-report comparison. These are possible work priorities, not salary or job guarantees."}}, "embedding_text": "ROLE\nName: Rain & Flood Expert\n\nCAREER CONTEXT\nIndustry: Water & Environmental Services\nDomain: Hydrology & Watershed Science\nRole Family: Hydrologist\n\nROLE SUMMARY\nStudies rain, river runoff and land cover to explain water movement and possible flood-related risks. Future role: Hydrologist; these school models do not predict real floods.\n\nWORK CONTEXT\nA watershed or hydrology team needs fair rainfall-runoff comparisons and repeated data before giving advice about river flow, erosion and possible flood impacts.\n\nTYPICAL WORK ACTIVITIES\nCompare two field reports and identify non-matched conditions; Set up a matched bare-soil versus leaf-cover runoff comparison; Average three model runoff trials for each condition; Compute runoff percentages and state the percentage-point difference without overclaiming soil loss\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES & ACTIONS\nCompare the Two Field Reports: align source ID, conditions, observations and missing fields side by side; identify which differences can be compared fairly; Build a Matched Runoff Comparison: compare the trays, keep the input and slope conditions matched, collect runoff separately and log source-specific readings; Calculate Runoff Across Three Trials: calculate means 160 mL and 100 mL; compute 64% and 40% runoff; report the 24-percentage-point gap\n\nDELIVERABLES & OUTPUTS\nField-report comparison; Matched-tray method and reading log; Three-trial average calculation; Runoff percentage and limitation report; Learning modules: RMR-CAP-L03-M01 - Compare the Two Field Reports (Core, step 1), RMR-CAP-L03-M02 - Build a Matched Runoff Comparison (Important, step 2), RMR-CAP-L03-M03 - Calculate Runoff Across Three Trials (Important, step 3)\n\nINTEREST AND WORK-STYLE ALIGNMENT\nInvestigative work interprets rainfall and runoff; Realistic work involves physical river and land conditions; Conventional methods require consistent trial records and units.\n\nAPTITUDE ALIGNMENT\nKey areas: Data Interpretation, Numerical Reasoning, Logical Reasoning\nReadiness: Rain & Flood Expert uses data interpretation, numerical reasoning, logical reasoning to compare two field reports and identify non-matched conditions, set up a matched bare-soil versus leaf-cover runoff comparison, and interpret source-based records. These priorities are proposed role demands, not measured learner aptitude.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL ALIGNMENT\nKey traits: Openness, Conscientiousness, Emotional Stability\nWork style: Rain & Flood Expert benefits from openness, conscientiousness, emotional stability when performing set up a matched bare-soil versus leaf-cover runoff comparison and following through on runoff percentage and limitation report. Traits guide supportive coaching, not exclusion.\n\nWORK-VALUE ALIGNMENT\nKey values: Impact, Autonomy, Security\nMotivation: This pathway may reward impact, autonomy, security through the work of compare two field reports and identify non-matched conditions and producing a clear field-report comparison. These are possible work priorities, not salary or job guarantees.\n\nEDUCATION AND ELIGIBILITY\nGate: Preferred\nStreams: B.Tech. Civil Engineering; B.Sc. Geography; B.Sc. Geology; M.Sc. Hydrology\n"}'::jsonb;
